  "answer": "The official 2026 pricing policy (effective June 1, 2026) supersedes and replaces the deprecated 2025 pricing proposal, which was rejected and retired for being financially unsustainable [NL-003-S01][NL-003-S08][NL-004-S01]. For each plan, the active policy raises both the monthly subscription rate and the one-time onboarding fee:\n\n- **Starter Plan**: Monthly price increased from $900 to $1,200; onboarding fee increased from $1,500 to $2,500 [NL-004-S05][NL-004-S02].\n- **Growth Plan**: Monthly price increased from $2,800 to $3,600; onboarding fee increased from $4,500 to $7,500 [NL-004-S05][NL-004-S02][NL-003-S08].\n- **Enterprise Plan**: Starting monthly price increased from $6,000 to $8,500; onboarding fee increased from $10,000 to a minimum of $15,000 [NL-004-S05][NL-004-S02].\n\nThe 2025 proposal also included per‑plan inclusions (e.g., Starter: 500 learners, 3 admin seats, email support; Growth: 2,000 learners, 10 admin seats, priority support; Enterprise: custom capacities, dedicated CSM) [NL-004-S02]. The 2026 policy does not list those inclusions in the provided evidence, but the pricing changes are explicitly stated. The 2025 rates are fully obsolete and must not be used in active agreements [NL-004-S02][NL-004-S01].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
